<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!-- ============================================================================================
     CloudKit-enabled entitlements (Phase 7A) — READY TO ACTIVATE, NOT the default.

     This is the app-group entitlements PLUS the CloudKit + push entitlements SwiftData needs to
     mirror the store into the user's private iCloud database. It is kept separate from the default
     `App.entitlements` on purpose:

       • Provisioning a CloudKit container requires a PAID Apple Developer Program membership
         ($99/yr). A free Apple ID / personal team CANNOT sign an app that declares these keys —
         attempting to sideload it on the free tier fails at signing. The whole project defaults to
         free-tier sideloading (LOCKED_DECISIONS #2), so the default build must NOT declare CloudKit.

     To ACTIVATE sync (after enrolling in the paid program and creating the container — see
     docs/CLOUDKIT_SETUP.md), do ONE of:
       (a) In Xcode, select the PersonalOpsAgent target → Signing & Capabilities → + Capability →
           iCloud → check "CloudKit" and add the container `iCloud.com.rajatarora.PersonalOpsAgent`.
           Xcode rewrites `App.entitlements` for you; you can then delete this file.
       (b) Point the target's build setting `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS` at this file:
           `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = App/App.CloudKit.entitlements` (Debug + Release).
     Then set `CLOUDKIT_SYNC_ENABLED=true` in `Secrets/Config.local` and run on a signed device.
     ============================================================================================ -->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.rajatarora.PersonalOpsAgent</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.com.rajatarora.PersonalOpsAgent</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
	<array>
		<string>CloudKit</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Push entitlement drives CloudKit's near-real-time sync notifications. On a paid account
	     Xcode/automatic-signing provisions this; change to `production` for a release build. -->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
</dict>
</plist>
